  "description": "An amount that fills the mask, and the high-order truncation the double add then causes. 999999999.99 renders as ' 999,999,999.99' in the detail's - mask and '+999,999,999.99' in the totals' + mask, with no suppression anywhere and both commas printing. Then defect 2 adds the same amount to WS-PAGE-TOTAL a second time at :200: the sum is 1999999999.98, which does not fit the nine integer digits of PIC S9(09)V99, and COBOL stores it without ON SIZE ERROR by discarding the high-order digit - so the page total, and through :297 the grand total, print 999,999,999.98 rather than the mathematical sum. Truncation, never rounding: ROUNDED appears zero times in all 28 programs.",
